The  driver  handles all Bluetooth Human Interface Devices.  Each
HID device can have several components, e.g., a  keyboard  and  a
mouse.  These components use different report identifiers to dis‐
tinguish  which  component  data  is coming from.  The driver may
have several children attached that handle particular  components
and  dispatches  data  to them based on the report id.  Normally,
Bluetooth HIDs will be attached using the program.  The following
properties are used by the driver during autoconfiguration: Local
device address.  Remote device address.  The driver  matches  the
